docs/fidelity.md:86:- Player Rocket Launcher3015 (`_‑VG`) uses `Timer(100,10)`: first shot100ms after activation, then ten callbacks at100ms spacing, with emitters1–5 repeated and current muzzle/rotation sampled on each callback. The timer continues through jam/stun/pause. Ordinary crossing `_‑ZY → _‑1J` and avatar replacement cancel it; level-zero `_‑1E(true)` bypasses FinalPartCall. Rejected transit callbacks are consumed, not replayed after arrival. Enemy4020 remains part-clocked, retaining its six-call interval between bursts.
