docs/fidelity.md:143:- The HUD fixture covers nine unique rows, repeated primaries, secondary-only and empty-weapon layouts, and partial life/cooldowns. Filled/empty alpha samples were 193/51 for primary/secondary bars and 158/40 for life, verifying the original child/root alpha combination and scale overwrite. Six rule tests cover source easing/order, idle timing, first-mount grouping, held-input behavior, and paused/transit clocks. These prove recovered contracts and artwork placement, not whole-HUD pixel identity.
docs/fidelity.md:182:- Eight source-contract regressions cover callback selection, absence of invented rings, paused playback/polling, shared crossing layers/arrival removal, connected rocket segments, teleport positions/order, burst radius, Ripple and Neutralizer clocks. The isolated browser fixture checks native/mock trail alpha at frames1/13/25, cleanup on resume, nonempty output for all12 roots, and upper/lower occlusion. Native trail samples agree with30%/15%/0 alpha. The gallery was visually inspected. These are deterministic reconstruction checks, not Adobe Flash pixel identity.
docs/fidelity.md:202:- `tools/import-mine-art.ts` recovers only numerical IDs/counts/labels from the local SWF. Seeker2178 arms at41, frame40 jumps to1 and rerolls a rounded0…10 start, and55 stops without expiring or stopping homing. The root MovieClip clock continues during gameplay pause/collapse/crossing. Ordinary enemy1792 and ally2182 inherit `_‑BL.frame1` random starts and loop16→2. Ally2182 removes every child at7, intentionally blinking until the loop returns to2. No artwork is exported. Exact Flash behavior for randomized frame0, independently randomized child clocks and stage event interleaving remains unverified.
